     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written (Order ID: ORD-0001): amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily.\n\n- **Flag on the order:** I added a note that the dose is above the 10 mg/day labeled maximum. The note also says the order needs attending or pharmacist review, and that the patient needs monitoring of BP, heart rate, and peripheral edema.\n- **Attending review:** You confirmed the order, but you didn't say that your attending or a pharmacist approved it. Please make sure your supervising physician reviews it soon. Pharmacy may contact the team to verify the dose.\n- **Monitoring:** Watch closely for hypotension, dizziness, tachycardia, and swelling in the legs and ankles, especially after the first doses."
